# =============================================================================
# Intelli-Scan Backend — Environment Variables
# =============================================================================
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values before running the server.
# Never commit the filled-in .env file to version control.
#
# =============================================================================
# GitHub App Configuration
# =============================================================================
#
# How to create a GitHub App
# --------------------------
# 1. Go to your GitHub profile or organisation → Settings → Developer settings
#    → GitHub Apps → New GitHub App.
# 2. Set the "Webhook URL" to: https://<your-domain>/webhooks/github
# 3. Set a "Webhook secret" (any random string) — this becomes GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
# 4. Under "Repository permissions" enable:
#    - Contents: Read & Write        (needed to commit patches)
#    - Pull requests: Read & Write   (needed to open PRs and post review comments)
# 5. Under "Subscribe to events" tick: Pull request
# 6. After creating the app, note the App ID from the General settings page.
# 7. Under "Private keys" generate and download an RSA private key (.pem file).
#    Paste its content as GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY (keep the header/footer lines).
# 8. Install the app on the repositories you want Intelli-Scan to scan.
#    The installation ID is visible in the webhook payload under `installation.id`.
#
# Where to find each value
# ------------------------
# GITHUB_APP_ID            → General tab of your App settings page (numeric ID).
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY   → Generate under "Private keys" on the General tab.
# GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET → The secret you typed when creating the webhook.
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID     → "Client ID" on the General tab (for OAuth).
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET → Generate under "Client secrets" on the General tab.

GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----
...
-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"
GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# Existing variables — already present, do not remove
# =============================================================================

# PostgreSQL connection string.
# Local example:  postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/intelliscan
# Heroku example: postgres://...  (Heroku sets this automatically)
DATABASE_URL=

# Google Gemini API key(s) — comma-separated to enable key rotation.
# Obtain from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
